<header><p class="st-kicker">county · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Vaudémont</h1><p class="st-meta">1070 CE – 1473 CE (approx.) · capital Vaudémont</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Lorraine county held by a cadet line of the ducal house, whose heir René II finally inherited the Duchy of Lorraine itself.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1070 Duke Gerard of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine's</a> younger son Gerard received the county of Vaudémont, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nancy">Nancy</a>, with its castle on the hill of Sion. His descendants ruled it as a cadet branch, often at odds with the main ducal line.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Vaudémont was a modest rural county whose hill of Sion was a Marian pilgrimage site. In the 14th century it passed to the house of Joinville and then, by marriage, to Ferry of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-lorraine">Lorraine</a>. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antoine-of-vaudemont">Antoine of Vaudémont</a> claimed the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> and defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rene-of-anjou">René of Anjou</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bulgneville">Bulgnéville</a> in 1431.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Antoine's son Ferry II married René's daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yolande-duchess-of-lorraine">Yolande</a>, and their son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rene-ii-duke-of-lorraine">René II</a> inherited the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-lorraine">Duchy of Lorraine</a> in 1473, merging Vaudémont with it. The title survived as a dignity for younger members of the ducal family.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="county, 1070 CE – 1473 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">county</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st